{"id":"0c82f083-1a20-44c3-990f-d17dbd14e0e6","object":"chat.completion","created":1785001972,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\\n    root_id = None\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is None:\\n            root_id = n['id']\\n        else:\\n            children.setdefault(n['parent'], []).append(n['id'])\\n\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    candidates = []\\n    for nid, n in node_map.items():\\n        if nid == root_id:\\n            continue\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if n['symbol'] in required:\\n            continue\\n        candidates.append((n['depth'], nid))\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n    for depth, nid in candidates:\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        has_retained_child = any(child in retained for child in children.get(nid, []))\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbols_present = set()\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            symbols_present.add(node_map[rid]['symbol'])\\n        if required.issubset(symbols_present):\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_sorted\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for SE-PE-01 based on the described process: \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\". The case payload contains nodes (list of objects with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) and required_symbols (list of strings). The task is to reduce the parse tree by removing removable nodes while preserving that all required symbols are still represented somewhere in the tree, and respecting that we cannot remove nodes that have retained children. Also, we must consider deeper nodes first, then by depth, then tie-break by node ID. The output should have removed_node_ids (list of IDs in removal order) and retained_node_ids (sorted list of IDs of nodes that remain).\n\nWe need to implement a traversal that decides which nodes to remove. The objective: reduce the tree by removing removable nodes if possible without losing required symbols. Also, we cannot remove a node if any of its children are retained? Actually \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" Means if a node has any child that is retained (i.e., not removed), then you cannot remove it. So removal must be from leaves upward, but also considering that if you remove a leaf that is required symbol, you cannot. So we need to process nodes in order: deeper first (higher depth), then maybe within same depth, some order? The spec says \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" and \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" So we need to sort nodes by depth descending, then by ID ascending (or descending? \"tie break\" typically ascending for stability). Also \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we must check after removal, the set of symbols present among retained nodes still includes all required symbols.\n\nThe process: start with all nodes retained. Then iterate over nodes in the specified order. For each node that is removable and not root (root has parent null), check if it has any children that are currently retained. If yes, skip. Then tentatively remove it (mark as removed) and check if required symbols are still covered by remaining retained nodes. If yes, commit removal; otherwise, keep it.\n\nFinally, output sorted retained node IDs (alphabetically? The spec doesn't specify sorting order for retained_node_ids, but likely sorted by some consistent order. Since it's a list of strings, \"sorted\" probably means lexicographic ascending. The example outputs in other tasks often sorted. We'll sort ascending.\n\nFor removed_node_ids: the order of removal as we processed them (the order we actually removed). That should be the order in which we iterate and remove, which is depth descending, tie-break by ID ascending.\n\nEdge cases: root has parent null and is non-removable; required_symbols list includes symbols that must be present. We need to check after removal that each required symbol appears in at least one retained node. Also, we cannot remove a node if it has retained children; so we must check children that are still retained (not yet removed). Since we process deeper first, when we consider a parent, its children may have already been removed if they qualified. So if all children are removed, then parent may become removable if none of its children are retained.\n\nCheck the fixture data: nodes have ids like root, n1, n2, etc. removable flags. Required symbols: root, s1.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) that returns {\"removed_node_ids\": [...], \"retained_node_ids\": [...]}.\n\nImplementation: parse case['nodes'] into dict id->node. Build children map: for each node, add to parent's children list. Then get root node (the one with parent null). Then sort nodes (excluding root? Actually root is not removable, but we include in sorting? It will never be removed, but we can include it; we'll skip if not removable. Better to sort all nodes, but skip root and non-removable in loop. For sorting: we need to ensure we process deeper depth first. We'll create a list of node IDs that are removable (excluding root) sorted by depth descending, then by ID ascending. Then iterate. For each node, check if any of its children are still in retained set. Initially retained set is all node IDs. We'll maintain a set of retained IDs. For each candidate, if its children (from children map) have any intersection with retained set, skip. Else, tentatively remove it: remove from retained set, then check required symbols: for each required symbol, check if there exists any retained node with that symbol. If all present, commit removal and record node ID in removed list. If any missing, revert: add back to retained set. Continue.\n\nFinally, after loop, retained_node_ids sorted ascending, removed_node_ids in removal order.\n\nCheck: The spec says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So we also must ensure we don't remove nodes with symbol in required_symbols, even if removable flag is true? The fixture shows that some required symbols appear on non-removable nodes (like n1 has symbol s1 and removable=false). But what if a required symbol appears on a removable node? The spec says required symbol nodes cannot be removed. So we need to explicitly skip nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols.\n\nThus condition: if node.symbol in required_symbols: skip even if removable. Also if node is root (id == root? Actually root is identified by parent null, but we could also check id == 'root'? Safer to check parent is None). Root may have symbol root and required_symbols includes 'root', so it's already covered.\n\nImplementation details: The payload includes _case_nonce but we ignore.\n\nReturn JSON object with list of strings.\n\nWe must not mutate case; we'll work on copies.\n\nWrite Python code inside solve(case). Use only standard library.\n\nNow format as JSON string for \"implementation\".\n\nMake sure the output follows the exact output schema: { \"removed_node_ids\": [...], \"retained_node_ids\": [...] }\n\nTest with given fixtures: For first case, we need to compute. We'll implement and then produce the code.\n\nLet's write pseudocode:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required = set(case['required_symbols'])\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_map}\n    root_id = None\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n['parent'] is None:\n            root_id = n['id']\n        else:\n            children.setdefault(n['parent'], []).append(n['id'])\n    \n    # Initialize retained set with all node ids\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\n    # Candidate nodes: removable, not root, symbol not in required\n    candidates = []\n    for nid, n in node_map.items():\n        if nid == root_id: continue\n        if not n['removable']: continue\n        if n['symbol'] in required: continue\n        candidates.append((n['depth'], nid))\n    # Sort by depth descending, then id ascending\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    for depth, nid in candidates:\n        # Check if node still retained (it might have been removed earlier)\n        if nid not in retained:\n            continue\n        # Check children: any child still retained?\n        has_retained_child = any(child in retained for child in children.get(nid, []))\n        if has_retained_child:\n            continue\n        # Tentatively remove\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        # Check required symbols\n        symbols_present = set()\n        for rid in retained:\n            symbols_present.add(node_map[rid]['symbol'])\n        if required.issubset(symbols_present):\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # revert\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    # After loop, retained set is final\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n\nThat should work.\n\nNow we need to output as JSON with key \"implementation\" and the Python code as a string.\n\nWe'll write the code with proper indentation.\n\nNote: The problem says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So removed_node_ids should be in order we removed, which matches the iteration order of candidates (depth descending, id ascending) but only those actually removed. That's correct.\n\nMake sure to handle case where a node's children list might be empty (leaf). Also handle nodes that have no children entry in children dict (but we initialized with empty list for each node, so safe).\n\nEdge: If a node is not removable but its symbol is required, we never attempt to remove it. Good.\n\nNow produce JSON response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2054,"completion_tokens":2274,"total_tokens":4328,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1877},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}